  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Upper level low pressure near Toronto Ontario \nearly today will drift northeast and diminish its influence on \nour cool temps and occasionally showery conditions through the \nmidweek period with a gradual warmup in temperatures Tuesday \nthrough Thursday. \n\nLeft exit region of an upper level jetlet rounding the base of \nthe upper trough combined with a CFA and sfc reflection in the \nform of a weak trough has led to areas of showers advecting \ninto South-Central PA and the Lower and Mid Susq Valley early \ntoday (and even a few low- topped TSRA a few hours ago near and \nto the North of KIPT).\n\nExpect a fair amount of morning sunshine across the bulk of\nCentral PA after this current, embedded shortwave trough exits\nto the east and NE later this morning. However, unseasonably\ncool temps aloft (850 temps mainly +8 to +9C today) will lead \nto the sunshine taking on a self destruct form with plenty of \nMDT CU/Thickening strato cu developing /advecting ESE from the \nNW Mtns twd the central ridge and valley region. The next \ncompact shortwave and mid/upper level speed max will rotate \nthrough a bit further to the north today, focusing the vast \nmajority of any showers near and to the north of the RT 6 \ncorridor in northern PA. \n\nAs noted in previous discussions and based on current high res\nensembles and its members, it's unlikely that any precip will \nget south of I-80, but there will be plenty of clouds. Some \nshowers will linger into the night and possibly early Tuesday \nbefore drier air works in as the upper trough departs.\n\nVertical mixing depth increasing to 4-6 kft after 14Z today will\nlead to a quick increase in the West to West-Southwest breeze \nwith moderate gusts into the upper teens at times. There will be\nnearly a 20 deg delta in max temps from North to South today, \nwith reading struggling to reach 60F across the highest terrain\nnear and north of RT 6, while the Lower Susq Valley sees \nafternoon highs in the mid to upper 70s. These high temps will \nbe 10-13F below normal across the Northern Tier counties and \njust a few degrees below normal in the Lower Susq Valley.",
